// Debug configurations, ported from `.vscode/launch.json`.
//
// NOTE: Zed ships no `cortex-debug` extension. The original configuration used
// cortex-debug + OpenOCD (`board/st_nucleo_f4.cfg`) to flash/debug an STM32.
// Zed's built-in C/C++ debug adapter is CodeLLDB (with GDB as a secondary
// adapter), and there is no one-to-one equivalent for cortex-debug's
// `servertype`, `liveWatch`, and `runToEntryPoint` features.
//
// The configuration below launches the built ELF through CodeLLDB. For
// on-target STM32 debugging, start the "openocd" task (`.zed/tasks.json`) to
// expose OpenOCD's GDB server (default port 3333), then attach a GDB/LLDB
// remote session to it; that wiring is adapter-specific and may need tuning.
[
  {
    "label": "Debug app.elf (CodeLLDB)",
    "adapter": "CodeLLDB",
    "request": "launch",
    "program": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/build/app.elf",
    "cwd": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT",
    "build": "build (full)"
  }
]
